          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP311 Fulton Park 

Out with the kids to find a few caps on this beautiful day.TFTBC!&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="684648200">
          <groundspeak:date>2017-05-06T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="946600">Black Shark</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP311 Fulton Park&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We had brought along the metal detector today because it appeared that some of the caps we hoped to find would be difficult to locate and had been problematic for others.  This was one of them.  On our way over we scanned for flagging tape but found none.  We would tie some up once we found the cap.  To our delight the cap was located quickly.  Although we both realized that we were having phenomenal luck, we carefully avoided mentioning it until we were finished for the day and past the point of jinxing ourselves, and the metal detector never left the vehicle!  &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We forgot about the flagging tape until we had driven away.  Oops.  &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;On our way to the next cap we spotted an apple tree in full bloom and two weddings!  Thanks for the cap and discoveries along the way, outforthehunt!&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="684124117">
          <groundspeak:date>2017-05-06T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="3339080">Gimli*/GeoJoce</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP311 Fulton Park&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Cap 5 of 7 today and this was one I had tried a few weeks earlier but hadn't found it.  I noticed that mkperry had found it recently so I decided to give it another go.  Their context picture helped immensely, and after a few minutes of studying and looking I found it!  Yes!!  So happy I gave this one another try today and was successful.  Thanks again OFTH!&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="682978492">
          <groundspeak:date>2017-05-01T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="7458582">mkPerry</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP311 Fulton Park 

Stopped for this one on the way home. Somebody has trimmed all the long grass which made the search somewhat easier. Saw a dent in the fallen grass at GZ and quickly uncovered the cap. &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Thanks outforthehunt for another BCP. &lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="633560776">
          <groundspeak:date>2016-08-30T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Didn't find it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="578246">BVPete</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BCP311 Fulton Park&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our one and only DNF today. Mrs BVPete and I gave it a good try, Jack the dog even tried to help, but to no avail. After about 20 minutes we gave up and headed to the next one on our list.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Thanks for posting the cap ofth.&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
